Given a List<Integer> and a target number, how would you find its index?
If there are multiple target number return highest index.
Null value possible.

Input List<Integer> iL = Arrays.asList(null,563, 234, 789, 234, 222, 234); Integer findNum = 234;
Output 2

============Top 5 solutions
1)List.indexOf() (the idiomatic answer)
int index = list.indexOf(target); // -1 if not found
O(n) time, O(1)

2)Manual loop
int fo=-1;
    int c=0;
    for(int i=0; i< iL.size();i++){
      if(Objects.equals(findNum, iL.get(i))){
        c++;
        fo=i;
      }
    }
    return fo;
O(n) time, O(1)

3. Streams
int index = IntStream.range(0, list.size())
        .filter(i -> Objects.equals(list.get(i), target))
        .findFirst()
        .orElse(-1);
O(n)

4. Binary search (only if the list is sorted)
java
int index = Collections.binarySearch(list, target);
if (index < 0) index = -1; // negative = not found (-(insertionPoint) - 1)
O(log n)

5. Precomputed HashMap (for repeated lookups)
java
Map<Integer, Integer> indexMap = new HashMap<>();
for (int i = 0; i < list.size(); i++) {
    indexMap.putIfAbsent(list.get(i), i); // keeps first occurrence
}
int index = indexMap.getOrDefault(target, -1);
O(n) to build, then O(1)